Both make sense.  Statistics from various public servers have
been discussed on RGRN over the years and it seems quite
consistant.

Soldier ants are one of the more powerfull monsters to appear
in groups and they are fast enough that it is easy to get caught
in a swarm.  You need to learn that when you see even one of
them it is time to retreat to a corridor and expect many.  Face
even one in the open and the rest will swarm you.  But they are
fast enough that they can swarm you before you reach a corridor.

Gnomes start out in the mines in swarms.  It is very easy to
start exploring a level of the mines and end up in a swarm of
them unable to retreat to the stairs.  It takes carefull and
conservative playing style to be able to survive the mines with
most of your characters.



